          "date": "2026-08-27 16:29:31.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Yonatan Nachum",
          "email": "ynachum@amazon.com",
          "date": "2026-08-27 17:32:11.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20655 efalnd: Fix wrong refcounting on launch Tx errors",
        "message": "LU-20655 efalnd: Fix wrong refcounting on launch Tx errors\n\nOn several flows like GETR ACK or FRWR completion we call launch Tx to\ncontinue to the next step stage of the Tx work. Those flows expect that\na refcount will be taken on the Tx in launch Tx before returning to the\ncaller or else it can potentially call Tx done function on a Tx that\nisn't completed yet. Launch Tx currently takes the refcount only when\nthe Tx was successfully posted to the device but this can fail if the QP\nis full or the connection isn't active.\n\nThis can lead to undefined behaviors on both sides of the transaction:\n- Initiator can potentially crash because of a race created between one\n  thread posting all pending TXs (including the one failed before) and\n  the thread completing the Tx.\n- Receiver can receive the done message without receiving the payload at\n  all.\n\nTo fix this, we take the Tx refcount once the Tx is placed on the\nconnection pending list. This means the Tx is committed to be sent\neventually (it can still be canceled). This eliminates the race since\nnow every Tx being sent by launch Tx has at least a single refcount.\n\nFixes: 0c773016d837 (\"LU-18977 efalnd: Introduce AWS EFA Lustre network driver\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\nChange-Id: I98c469d23780ab98520914905fca1b0100599103\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
